      "standardized_narrative": "The syndicate experienced a net prior year reserve release of GBP 27.6 million in 2014, driven by a favourable claims environment and over-provision for claims. This included reserve releases across Property Reinsurance, Energy Upstream, Political Risks, Terrorism, and Accident & Health. The 2008 underwriting year for International Casualty Reinsurance also saw positive settlements, and IBNR strengthening was reversed for the liability component of Specialty Programmes due to benign claims activity. While loss estimates for New Zealand earthquakes deteriorated for the 2012 YOA, this was offset by small improvements on other major losses such as Deepwater Horizon, the Japanese earthquake and tsunami, the Thailand Floods, and Super Storm Sandy.",
